    "# MGMT2D: Science and Strategy of AI\n",
    "## Lab 5: Building Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) for Image Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "Welcome to Lab 5! In this lab, you'll move from basic neural networks to **Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)**, the architecture that revolutionized computer vision. You'll work with the **CIFAR-10** dataset, a classic benchmark consisting of 60,000 small color images across 10 different classes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Your goal is to build, train, and compare several models, starting with a classic MLP to demonstrate why CNNs are uniquely powerful for image-based tasks. Finally, you'll see the power of massive, pre-trained models like ResNet and MobileNet on your own photos."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Learning Objectives\n",
    "- Understand the key differences between a classic MLP and a CNN for image data.\n",
    "- Implement foundational CNN layers like `Conv2D` and `MaxPooling2D`.\n",
    "- Build and compare CNN architectures of varying complexity.\n",
    "- Use pre-trained, state-of-the-art models (ResNet, MobileNet) for inference on custom images.\n",
    "- Discuss the trade-offs between model size, efficiency, and accuracy."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
