    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup and Data Preparation\n",
    "\n",
    "First, we'll import our libraries and load the CIFAR-10 dataset, which is conveniently available in Keras. We will normalize the pixel values and take a look at some of the images we'll be working with."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "from tensorflow import keras\n",
    "from keras import layers\n",
    "from keras.utils import plot_model\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, accuracy_score\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set random seeds for consistent results\n",
    "SEED = 42\n",
    "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "tf.random.set_seed(SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "# IMPORTANT FOR COLAB: To use a GPU, go to Runtime > Change runtime type and select T4 GPU.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define the class names for the 10 CIFAR categories\n",
    "CLASS_NAMES = [\n",
    "    'airplane', 'automobile', 'bird', 'cat', 'deer', \n",
    "    'dog', 'frog', 'horse', 'ship', 'truck'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load and prepare the CIFAR-10 data\n",
    "(x_train, y_train), (x_test, y_test) = keras.datasets.cifar10.load_data()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Normalize pixel values to be between 0 and 1\n",
    "x_train = x_train.astype(\"float32\") / 255.0\n",
    "x_test  = x_test.astype(\"float32\") / 255.0\n",
    "\n",
    "# Flatten the labels for sparse categorical crossentropy\n",
    "y_train = y_train.flatten()\n",
    "y_test  = y_test.flatten()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Data loaded and prepared. ✅\")\n",
    "print(f\"Training data shape: {x_train.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test data shape: {x_test.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Data Preview\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's visualize a few examples from the training set. Unlike MNIST, these are 32x32 pixel **color** images."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "for i in range(10):\n",
    "    plt.subplot(2, 5, i + 1)\n",
    "    plt.imshow(x_train[i])\n",
    "    plt.title(CLASS_NAMES[y_train[i]])\n",
    "    plt.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Baseline Model - Classic Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP)\n",
    "\n",
    "To understand the power of CNNs, we first need a baseline. We'll build a standard MLP, similar to the one used for Fashion-MNIST. This model will flatten the 3D image data into a 1D vector, losing all spatial structure. Its performance will highlight why specialized architectures are needed for image tasks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define the baseline MLP architecture\n",
    "mlp_model = keras.Sequential([\n",
    "    layers.Input(shape=(32, 32, 3)),\n",
    "    layers.Flatten(), # Flatten the 32x32x3 image into a 3072-element vector\n",
    "    layers.Dense(256, activation=\"relu\"),\n",
    "    layers.Dense(128, activation=\"relu\"),\n",
    "    layers.Dense(10, activation=\"softmax\")\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "mlp_model.compile(optimizer=\"adam\", loss=\"sparse_categorical_crossentropy\", metrics=[\"accuracy\"])\n",
    "plot_model(mlp_model, show_shapes=True, show_layer_activations=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define callbacks and plotting function\n",
    "early_stopping = keras.callbacks.EarlyStopping(monitor=\"val_accuracy\", patience=5, restore_best_weights=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "def plot_history(history, title):\n",
    "    fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "    fig.suptitle(title, fontsize=16)\n",
    "    ax1.plot(history.history['accuracy'], label='Train')\n",
    "    ax1.plot(history.history['val_accuracy'], label='Validation')\n",
    "    ax1.set_title('Model Accuracy'); ax1.set_ylabel('Accuracy'); ax1.set_xlabel('Epoch'); ax1.legend(); ax1.grid(True)\n",
    "    ax2.plot(history.history['loss'], label='Train')\n",
    "    ax2.plot(history.history['val_loss'], label='Validation')\n",
    "    ax2.set_title('Model Loss'); ax2.set_ylabel('Loss'); ax2.set_xlabel('Epoch'); ax2.legend(); ax2.grid(True)\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Training Baseline MLP...\")\n",
    "history_mlp = mlp_model.fit(\n",
    "    x_train, y_train, \n",
    "    epochs=50, \n",
    "    batch_size=128, \n",
    "    validation_split=0.15, # Use part of the training data for validation\n",
    "    callbacks=[early_stopping],\n",
    "    verbose=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"Training complete. ✅\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "test_loss_mlp, test_acc_mlp = mlp_model.evaluate(x_test, y_test, verbose=0)\n",
    "print(f\"Baseline MLP - Test Accuracy: {test_acc_mlp*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "plot_history(history_mlp, \"Baseline MLP\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Building Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) 🧠\n",
    "\n",
    "The MLP struggled because it ignores the spatial relationships between pixels. A **Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)** is designed specifically for this. It uses learnable filters to scan for patterns (edges, textures, shapes) directly within the image structure.\n",
    "\n",
    "We will build two CNNs:\n",
    "- **Model 1**: A small, simple CNN to introduce the core concepts.\n",
    "- **Model 2**: A more advanced CNN using Dropout and Batch Normalization."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### CNN Model 1: Small CNN\n",
    "\n",
    "This model introduces two key CNN layers:\n",
    "- **`Conv2D`**: The convolutional layer that applies filters to the image.\n",
    "- **`MaxPooling2D`**: Downsamples the image to reduce computational load and focus on the most important features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define the small CNN architecture\n",
    "cnn_model_1 = keras.Sequential([\n",
    "    layers.Input(shape=(32, 32, 3)),\n",
    "    layers.Conv2D(32, 3, padding=\"same\", activation=\"relu\"),\n",
    "    layers.MaxPooling2D(),\n",
    "    layers.Conv2D(64, 3, padding=\"same\", activation=\"relu\"),\n",
    "    layers.MaxPooling2D(),\n",
    "    layers.Flatten(),\n",
    "    layers.Dense(128, activation=\"relu\"),\n",
    "    layers.Dense(10, activation=\"softmax\")\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "cnn_model_1.compile(optimizer=\"adam\", loss=\"sparse_categorical_crossentropy\", metrics=[\"accuracy\"])\n",
    "plot_model(cnn_model_1, show_shapes=True, show_layer_activations=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Training Small CNN...\")\n",
    "history_cnn_1 = cnn_model_1.fit(\n",
    "    x_train, y_train, \n",
    "    epochs=50, \n",
    "    batch_size=128, \n",
    "    validation_split=0.15,\n",
    "    callbacks=[early_stopping],\n",
    "    verbose=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"Training complete. ✅\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "test_loss_cnn_1, test_acc_cnn_1 = cnn_model_1.evaluate(x_test, y_test, verbose=0)\n",
    "print(f\"Small CNN - Test Accuracy: {test_acc_cnn_1*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "plot_history(history_cnn_1, \"Small CNN\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### CNN Model 2: Advanced CNN with Regularization\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we build a deeper and more robust CNN. This architecture includes:\n",
    "- **Deeper Layers**: More convolutional layers to learn a richer hierarchy of features.\n",
    "- **Batch Normalization**: Stabilizes and speeds up training.\n",
    "- **Dropout**: A regularization technique to prevent overfitting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define the advanced CNN architecture\n",
    "cnn_model_2 = keras.Sequential([\n",
    "    layers.Input(shape=(32, 32, 3)),\n",
    "    layers.Conv2D(32, 3, padding=\"same\", use_bias=False), \n",
    "    layers.BatchNormalization(), \n",
    "    layers.ReLU(),\n",
    "    layers.Conv2D(32, 3, padding=\"same\", use_bias=False), \n",
    "    layers.BatchNormalization(), \n",
    "    layers.ReLU(),\n",
    "    layers.MaxPooling2D(), \n",
    "    layers.Dropout(0.25),\n",
    "\n",
    "    layers.Conv2D(64, 3, padding=\"same\", use_bias=False), \n",
    "    layers.BatchNormalization(), \n",
    "    layers.ReLU(),\n",
    "    layers.Conv2D(64, 3, padding=\"same\", use_bias=False), \n",
    "    layers.BatchNormalization(), \n",
    "    layers.ReLU(),\n",
    "    layers.MaxPooling2D(), \n",
    "    layers.Dropout(0.25),\n",
    "\n",
    "    layers.Flatten(),\n",
    "    layers.Dense(128, activation=\"relu\"), \n",
    "    layers.Dropout(0.4),\n",
    "    layers.Dense(10, activation=\"softmax\")\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "cnn_model_2.compile(optimizer=\"adam\", loss=\"sparse_categorical_crossentropy\", metrics=[\"accuracy\"])\n",
    "plot_model(cnn_model_2, show_shapes=True, show_layer_activations=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Training Advanced CNN...\")\n",
    "history_cnn_2 = cnn_model_2.fit(\n",
    "    x_train, y_train, \n",
    "    epochs=50, \n",
    "    batch_size=128, \n",
    "    validation_split=0.15,\n",
    "    callbacks=[early_stopping],\n",
    "    verbose=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(\"Training complete. ✅\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "test_loss_cnn_2, test_acc_cnn_2 = cnn_model_2.evaluate(x_test, y_test, verbose=0)\n",
    "print(f\"Advanced CNN - Test Accuracy: {test_acc_cnn_2*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "plot_history(history_cnn_2, \"Advanced CNN\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Exploring State-of-the-Art Pre-trained Models\n",
    "\n",
    "Training a highly accurate CNN from scratch requires massive datasets (like ImageNet with over 1 million images) and significant computational power. A common and powerful strategy is to use a **pre-trained model** that has already learned rich features from a large dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "We will now explore two famous pre-trained architectures:\n",
    "- **ResNet50**: A very deep (50-layer) and highly accurate model known for its use of \"residual connections\" that help it learn effectively despite its depth.\n",
    "- **MobileNetV2**: A lightweight, highly efficient model designed to run quickly on mobile devices and other systems with limited computational power. It achieves impressive accuracy with a fraction of the parameters of larger models.\n",
    "\n",
    "The following code will load both models with weights pre-trained on the ImageNet dataset and allow you to classify your own images. This process is called **inference**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from tensorflow.keras.applications import resnet50, mobilenet_v2\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.preprocessing import image\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, HTML\n",
    "import ipywidgets as widgets\n",
    "import io\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load pre-trained models\n",
    "print(\"Loading ResNet50 and MobileNetV2 models...\")\n",
    "resnet_model = resnet50.ResNet50(weights=\"imagenet\")\n",
    "mobilenet_model = mobilenet_v2.MobileNetV2(weights=\"imagenet\")\n",
    "print(\"Models loaded. ✅\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Function to preprocess image and make predictions\n",
    "def predict_image(img_bytes):\n",
    "    img = Image.open(io.BytesIO(img_bytes)).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
    "    img_resized = img.resize((224, 224)) # Both models expect 224x224 input\n",
    "    img_array = image.img_to_array(img_resized)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Predictions for MobileNetV2\n",
    "    mobilenet_input = mobilenet_v2.preprocess_input(np.expand_dims(img_array.copy(), axis=0))\n",
    "    mobilenet_preds = mobilenet_model.predict(mobilenet_input)\n",
    "    decoded_mobilenet = mobilenet_v2.decode_predictions(mobilenet_preds, top=5)[0]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Predictions for ResNet50\n",
    "    resnet_input = resnet50.preprocess_input(np.expand_dims(img_array.copy(), axis=0))\n",
    "    resnet_preds = resnet_model.predict(resnet_input)\n",
    "    decoded_resnet = resnet50.decode_predictions(resnet_preds, top=5)[0]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return img, decoded_mobilenet, decoded_resnet\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create the upload widget and display\n",
    "uploader = widgets.FileUpload(accept='image/*', multiple=False)\n",
    "output_area = widgets.Output()\n",
    "\n",
    "def on_upload(change):\n",
    "    if not change['new']:\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    uploaded_file = uploader.value\n",
    "    # The file object is a dictionary, get the content\n",
    "    file_content = list(uploaded_file.values())[0]['content']\n",
    "    img, mobilenet_top5, resnet_top5 = predict_image(file_content)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    with output_area:\n",
    "        output_area.clear_output()\n",
    "        print(\"--- PREDICTIONS ---\")\n",
    "        display(img.resize((200, 200)))\n",
    "        print(\"\\nMobileNetV2 Top 5:\")\n",
    "        for _, name, score in mobilenet_top5:\n",
    "            print(f\"  - {name}: {score:.2%}\")\n",
    "        print(\"\\nResNet50 Top 5:\")\n",
    "        for _, name, score in resnet_top5:\n",
    "            print(f\"  - {name}: {score:.2%}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "uploader.observe(on_upload, names='_counter')\n",
    "display(HTML(\"<b>Upload an image to classify:</b>\"))\n",
    "display(uploader, output_area)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
